        "ended_at": "2026-08-27T14:23:59.000Z",
        "title": "Global command palette on Cmd/Ctrl+K",
        "summary": "A first-class launcher spanning recent chats, apps, projects, agents, and menu actions arrives in the Aura shell.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added a global command palette wired into AuraShell that searches recent chats, apps, projects, agents, and menu actions with keyboard navigation, disabled-action filtering, and a `>` prefix for action-only results.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "3cdf448fb4426d0f7b33e576a101937897e68cf2"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Extended the MenuBar registry and a new UI modal store so the palette reuses canonical Aura routes and existing action handlers rather than introducing a parallel navigation system.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "3cdf448fb4426d0f7b33e576a101937897e68cf2"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Published a T3 Code reference audit documenting the gaps that motivated the palette and the source-control workbench, and confirming no upstream source was copied in.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "3cdf448fb4426d0f7b33e576a101937897e68cf2"
            ],
            "confidence": "medium"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "9:52 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-27T16:52:46.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-27T16:52:46.000Z",
        "title": "Preview browser routes to hosted local harness",
        "summary": "The remote Preview proxy now knows how to tunnel loopback dev-server URLs into a separately hosted local harness, not just a swarm agent.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Taught the browser spawn path to start a hosted-harness Preview proxy when a project is selected, failing closed with a clear service-unavailable error when the hosted tunnel is missing its transport auth.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "8529187b46b4986667561548497b1e68519dae51"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added a `hosted_preview_target` accessor on the harness gateway that only exposes hosted (non-loopback) bases with a transport bearer, keeping desktop loopback harnesses on their existing direct path.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "8529187b46b4986667561548497b1e68519dae51"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Generalized the remote preview proxy with a `PreviewTunnelTarget` abstraction so swarm agents and hosted harnesses share one SOCKS-over-WebSocket tunneling path to the machine that owns the dev server.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "8529187b46b4986667561548497b1e68519dae51"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "7:27 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-08-28T02:27:31.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-08-28T02:27:31.000Z",
        "title": "Native source-control workbench in the Sidekick",
        "summary": "A provider-neutral Git workbench lands in the Sidekick with status, diffs, staging, commits, and best-effort PR linking.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Introduced a `source_control` server handler exposing project-scoped Git status, staged/worktree diffs, stage/unstage, and commit operations with bounded limits on file counts, diff bytes, path batches, and commit message size.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "a0cbf0d18203655c16395f7fe0b07421d727c893"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Shipped a SourceControlWorkbench component and Sidekick taskbar entry that render branch, ahead/behind, changed files, and diffs, with an optional linked pull request surfaced as provider-tagged metadata.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "a0cbf0d18203655c16395f7fe0b07421d727c893"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Kept the HTTP contract provider-neutral so GitHub detection is best-effort today and additional review adapters (GitLab, Bitbucket, Azure DevOps) can slot in without changing the workbench response shape.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "a0cbf0d18203655c16395f7fe0b07421d727c893"
            ],
            "confidence": "medium"
          }
        ]
      }
